# Task 2: One-to-One Relationship

## Definition

A one-to-one relationship means each record in one table is related to only one record in another table.

Example:
User and Profile

## Implementation

It is implemented using a Foreign Key in one of the tables.

## Where to Place Join Column

The Foreign Key should be placed in the dependent table.

## Example

CREATE TABLE User (
id INT PRIMARY KEY
);

CREATE TABLE Profile (
id INT PRIMARY KEY,
user_id INT UNIQUE,
FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES User(id)
);

## Reason

Profile depends on User, so the foreign key is placed inside the Profile table.
